NAME
    trust - approve a module file you added, by its hash

SYNOPSIS
    trust <path>

DESCRIPTION
    Records a file's SHA-256 hash as approved, so that a command module
    you added to the shell can be loaded once loading one is supported:
    a module runs inside the program with your full permissions, and is
    approved once, by you, at the prompt. A changed file has another hash
    and must be approved again.

    The approval is given only at the prompt: 'trust' refuses inside a
    script run with 'source' and inside $(...), so a script cannot approve
    a file on your behalf. The path is resolved through the sandbox, as
    every path is (see 'man hier'). Approvals are kept, one hash and path
    to a line, in the 'trusted' file of the 'dianash' folder beside the
    program's configuration.

EXAMPLES
    trust /lib/dianash/mymodule.so
